  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="bef3-d9a2-c56b-5651" name="Ancient Chinese (Armies of Antiquity) - List Notes" publicationId="aab0-aa1e-0319-4ffe" hidden="false">
      <description>ANCIENT CHINESE ARMY LIST (Armies of Antiquity, pp.42-43), Chin and Han dynasties (500 BC - AD 300), with options for the Tang (AD 500-900).
Characters: the army must have a General (not enforced) and may have an Army Standard Bearer. Chariotry &amp; Cavalry up to a quarter of the points; Infantry at least a quarter; Allies &amp; Mercenaries up to a quarter; War Machines up to one per Halberdier or Spearman unit.
Rocket Artillery: rockets are war machines and follow the same general rules as stone throwers and bolt throwers for crew. Fired in the shooting phase: pick a direction and a fuse length 1-12 (the number of D6 thrown for the distance in inches). Roll the Scatter dice: on a Hit the rocket flies the rolled distance in the chosen direction; on a Scatter it flies off from its launcher in the direction of the arrow. Work out casualties with the circular template as for a stone thrower. Strength 5, negating armour saves. Any unit taking casualties from a rocket must take a Panic test or flee; cavalry, chariots and elephants test on 3D6 rather than 2D6.
Allies (not built here: make a separate small roster): from the Nomadic Hordes list.

ARMY COMPOSITION (percentages by points):
  Chariotry &amp; Cavalry: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
